oposal. Preserve every earlier assertion and timestamp. When dated_id_discrepancy explicitly records a main-reviewed same-listing reobservation, the older asserted IMDb is historical contrary evidence, not a simultaneous current ID conflict. Its evidence-present-by outcome time is an upper bound; its exact fetch time is unknown. Weigh the current matching identifiers, title and same-role people alongside that history. Explain the discrepancy in rationale, including both exact IMDb identifiers; do not infer source intent, historical falsity, physical media truth or automatic approval. A producer flag, reviewed historical discrepancy, missing director when cast corroborates, or missing cast when directors corroborate is not by itself an identity blocker. Missing a people subfield is not contrary evidence. If people overlap exists, a people blocker must identify a different material uncertainty beyond the absent subfield. Genuine current conflicts and inadequate identity evidence remain unresolved. Compare festival/theatrical years and runtime measurements in context; no invented tolerance, score or named-film exception. Matching IDs alone are insufficient. A supported proposal needs observed non-ID corroboration, the exact source/catalogue citations, no blockers and human review. Unresolved/blocked remains available: state at most two strongest material blockers. For each, support_considered must explain the strongest observed corroboration or its absence; material_conflict must explain the concrete competing claim or why the remaining uncertainty prevents a proposal after considering that support. Write complete concise sentences, not labels, fragments, repeated enums or lists of missing fields. Each justification may use up to400 characters. Rationale is at most600 characters, uncertainty at most300. Give evidence justifications, never internal reasoning. Do not force a supported result or reconstruct an earlier verdict. Physical edition, current queue, source indep